  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n // Common attributes\n \n-:wireshark-version: 4.4.8\n+:wireshark-version: 4.4.9\n :logray-version: 0.9.0\n \n // Required for btn, kbd:, and menu: macros.\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/attributes.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/attributes.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -40,16 +40,6 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark took a bite out of each of your freshly baked muffins until it found the perfect one.\n \n-* Renegotiated DTLS session is not being decrypted. wsbuglink:20362[].\n-* Wireshark is completely stuck in initialization because androiddump recv() is blocked. wsbuglink:20526[].\n-* Fuzz job UTF-8 encoding issue: fuzz-2025-06-20-7318.pcap. wsbuglink:20585[].\n-* Crash when showing packet in new window after reloading Lua plugins with a certain gui.column.format preference. wsbuglink:20588[].\n-* Bug in UDS dissector with Service ReadDataByPeriodicIdentifier Response. wsbuglink:20589[].\n-* Packet diagram doesn't show non-standard field value representations. wsbuglink:20590[].\n-* Packet diagram shows representation twice when field type is FT_NONE. wsbuglink:20601[].\n-* application/x-www-form-urlencoded key parsed incorrectly following a name-value byte sequence with no '=' wsbuglink:20615[].\n-* DNP3 time stamp was unable to work after epoch time(year 2038) wsbuglink:20618[].\n-\n // == Known Bugs\n \n === New and Updated Features\n@@ -68,33 +58,15 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.4.8.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-ASTERIX\n-DLT\n-DNP 3.0\n-DOF\n-DTLS\n-ETSI CAT\n-Gryphon\n-IPsec\n-ISObus VT\n-KRB5\n-MBIM\n-RTCP\n-SLL\n-STCSIG\n-TETRA\n-UDS\n-URL Encoded Form Data\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-[commaize]\n---\n-pcapng\n---\n+// [commaize]\n+// --\n+// --\n \n === Updated File Format Decoding Support\n \n@@ -112,6 +84,21 @@ There is no updated file format support in this release.\n \n == Prior Versions\n \n+Wireshark 4.4.8 included the following changes.\n+See the\n+https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.4.8.html[release notes]\n+for details:\n+\n+* Renegotiated DTLS session is not being decrypted. wsbuglink:20362[].\n+* Wireshark is completely stuck in initialization because androiddump recv() is blocked. wsbuglink:20526[].\n+* Fuzz job UTF-8 encoding issue: fuzz-2025-06-20-7318.pcap. wsbuglink:20585[].\n+* Crash when showing packet in new window after reloading Lua plugins with a certain gui.column.format preference. wsbuglink:20588[].\n+* Bug in UDS dissector with Service ReadDataByPeriodicIdentifier Response. wsbuglink:20589[].\n+* Packet diagram doesn't show non-standard field value representations. wsbuglink:20590[].\n+* Packet diagram shows representation twice when field type is FT_NONE. wsbuglink:20601[].\n+* application/x-www-form-urlencoded key parsed incorrectly following a name-value byte sequence with no '=' wsbuglink:20615[].\n+* DNP3 time stamp was unable to work after epoch time(year 2038) wsbuglink:20618[].\n+\n Wireshark 4.4.7 included the following changes.\n See the\n https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.4.7.html[release notes]\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/release-notes.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/release-notes.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -316,7 +316,7 @@ add_library(epan\n set_target_properties(epan PROPERTIES\n \tCOMPILE_DEFINITIONS \"WS_BUILD_DLL\"\n \tLINK_FLAGS \"${WS_LINK_FLAGS}\"\n-\tVERSION \"18.0.8\" SOVERSION 18\n+\tVERSION \"18.0.9\" SOVERSION 18\n \tINSTALL_RPATH \"${LIBRARY_INSTALL_RPATH}\"\n \t# By default the name for a library with target name epan will be libepan,\n \t# but Ethereal is now named Wireshark\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "epan/CMakeLists.txt",
